        "superseded_error": null,
        "superseded_justification": "Judge accepted the attributed review: mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_observation_outputevents.sql:9 casts outputevents.charttime through TIMESTAMPTZ, line 60 writes it to Observation.effectiveDateTime, and lines 62-65 write value to Observation.valueQuantity.value. The candidate reads those paths and applies the canonical item filters, 227488 negation, and SUM grouped by (stay_id, charttime). The comparator exhaustively attributes 393 only_oracle, 157 only_candidate, and 232 differing_conflict rows, including 236 key collisions, to the America/New_York DST-gap shift with zero residual; 393 shifted keys are 0.0118%, consistent with DST rarity. The original wall time is unrecoverable, no resource-id reconstruction is used, and identical fidelity is 3,321,123/3,321,748 (99.9812%) with no excluded columns.",
