        "superseded_error": null,
        "superseded_justification": "Judge accepted the attributed review: mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_observation_outputevents.sql:9 casts outputevents.charttime through TIMESTAMPTZ, line 60 writes the normalized value to Observation.effectiveDateTime, and lines 62-65 write valueQuantity.value. Attempt 0003 reads those paths with TIMESTAMP_NTZ, preserves all twelve item filters, applies the positive 227488 negation, and sums by stay_id and charttime. The comparator exhaustively attributes 393 only_oracle, 157 only_candidate, and 232 differing_conflict rows, including 236 occupied-key collisions, to the America/New_York DST-gap shift with zero residual; 393 shifted keys are 0.0118% of oracle rows, consistent with DST rarity. The original wall time is unrecoverable, resource IDs are opaque and were not inverted, and the contract accepts proven DST divergence including aggregation effects. Identical fidelity is 3,321,123/3,321,748 (99.9812%), with no excluded columns.",
